> chain3_A(x: u8) = x < 5 || x > 5
> chain3_B(x: u8) = x != 5
> equiv chain3_A ~ chain3_B
chain3_A and chain3_B are equal on the domain of chain3_A (exhaustive)
> chain4_A(x: u8) = 2 < x < 7 && x != 4
  note: chained comparison read as a conjunction
> chain4_B(x: u8) = x in 3..6 && x != 4
> equiv chain4_A ~ chain4_B
chain4_A and chain4_B are equal on the domain of chain4_A (exhaustive)
